{"rule_id": "reviewed-guarded-pattern:f4ff18466dbc0cfce0b075ac7dae052e0a42eee33e6ceebfb979c63f0cbbab37", "admission_code": "EXPLICIT_REVIEWED_RULE", "warrant": {"kind": "DEFINITIONAL_DERIVATION", "review_id": "linear-unit-want-proposal-review-2026-11-01", "reviewer": "Codex source-backed review; not independent semantic gold", "source_refs": ["docs/readings/2026-11-01-lexicon-next-stage/linear-unit-inventory.json", "docs/readings/2026-11-01-lexicon-next-stage/linear-unit-rule-ledger.md", "user-convention:WANT:-1=NOT_WANT,0=ORTHOGONAL,+1=WANT"], "statement": "In the inspected native linear-unit population, each exact noun sense denotes a specified metrological length, distance, or linear-density quantity. Its defining relation concerns magnitude and measurement, independent of an experiencer wanting or refusing it. This positive definitional independence warrants WANT=0 under the user polarity convention. Scope is exact native linear_unit.n.01 ancestry with matching identity and full definition, not all nouns or all measurement units. A native subtype whose own definition predicates desire/refusal would falsify this scope and require narrowing before use.", "warrant_id": "linear-unit-want-2026-11-01"}, "review": {"decision": "APPROVE_DEFINITIONAL_RULE", "rationale": "The exact native linear-unit definitions specify magnitude, length or linear density independently of an experiencer wanting or refusing it. All 56 source senses were inspected in the inventory; reviewed inch discovery and eight distinct held-out synsets agree with that interpretation, including mesh, head-based units, fistmele and combinatorial footer. Exact source identity and ancestry guards delimit the law; broader measurement classes and same-spelling senses are excluded. Admission is conditional and source-backed, not independent semantic gold. The failed BODY hypothesis is not admitted. Full-population migration and replay remain required.", "review_id": "linear-unit-want-admission-2026-11-01", "r