{"rule_id": "reviewed-guarded-pattern:65d16959c01e4411fe908f0a08ab3a0b130fa0cdf3095f20602b256862b56aa2", "admission_code": "EXPLICIT_REVIEWED_RULE", "warrant": {"kind": "DEFINITIONAL_DERIVATION", "review_id": "native-linear-unit-quantity-source-review-2026-11-01", "reviewer": "Codex primary source-backed review; not independent semantic gold", "source_refs": ["docs/readings/2026-11-01-lexicon-next-stage/quantity-unit-population-inventory.json@sha256:5a392a773cef5cebd2e9d05df34258bf17c35307cddd82d46be9dbb8134ced79", "docs/readings/2026-11-01-lexicon-you-body/you-body-reading.md", "data/external/references/goddard-2012-primes-molecules-templates.pdf#section-3", "gse/curation/lexicon_builder/foundation.py#projection_relations", "docs/readings/2026-11-01-lexicon-you-body/linear-unit-native-lemma-scope.json"], "statement": "Every inspected exact native linear-unit sense denotes a metrological magnitude: a specified length or distance, a magnitude expressed in such units, or the count per linear inch in mesh. QUANTITY=+1 expresses this own-definition quantitative content without setting a size sign, numerical value, anatomical value, or ordinal. Scope requires noun POS and verified complete native linear_unit.n.01 ancestry tied to the exact definition. All 56 complete definitions and examples were read; discovery and held-out distinct-synset model audit remain separate. No other measurement branch, homograph, or world-associated quantity is admitted. A native subtype lacking this quantitative meaning falsifies the proposed scope. Additional identity guard: the spelling must occur explicitly in the same native synset lemma_names, with casefold/underscore-space normalization only. This restricts the inspected population to 100 entries; the other 33 derived spellings are deferred for separate identity justification, not declared false. The previous ancestry-only proposal is superseded for admission.", "warrant_id": "native-linear-unit-quantity-2026-11-01"}, "review": {"decision": "APPROVE_DEFINITIONAL_RULE", "rationale": "The reviewed 56 native linear-unit definitions encode metrological magnitude, including amount in length units and count per linear inch. The exact native-lemma identity guard limits this derivation to 100 entries and defers 33 derived spellings. All eight distinct-synset held-out questions returned QUANTITY=+1 with no null, disagreement, or staging conflict, with the candidate relation and target assignment withheld. This warrants QUANTITY content only, not a numerical amount, size, bodily content, or an extension to the broader measurement ancestor. Prior source review and these audits are named evidence, not independent semantic gold.", "review_id": "native-linear-unit-quantity-admission-2026-11-01", "reviewer": "Codex primary source-backed review; not independent semantic gold", "rule_id": "reviewed-guarded-pattern:65d16959c01e4411fe908f0a08ab3a0b130fa0cdf3095f20602b256862b56aa2", "source_refs": ["docs/readings/2026-11-01-lexicon-you-body/you-body-reading.md", "docs/readings/2026-11-01-lexicon-you-body/linear-unit-native-lemma-scope.json", "docs/readings/2026-11-01-lexicon-you-body/linear-unit-quantity-audit.json", "docs/readings/2026-11-01-lexicon-you-body/quantity-discovery-source-review.json"], "warrant_sha256": "7734adc5cf42a3fce86a013df3ce152ea06c4c4ac06b498a6131f8272a0440e3"}, "audit_schema": {"audit_entry_ids": ["list", 8], "authority": ["str", 69], "candidates": ["list", 1], "discovery_entry_ids": ["list", 1], "format": ["str", 29], "input_sha256": ["str", 64], "lexicon_writes": ["bool", false], "max_model_calls": ["int", 8], "model_calls": ["int", 8], "repeated_audit_requests": ["list", 0], "unsupported": ["list", 4]}, "relation_matches_current": true}
{"rule_id": "reviewed-guarded-pattern:3bf66d8b1cf0cf629d8bd968d3a5e7cdcfee5b508d007afcd49793d8b4bbace1", "admission_code": "EXPLICIT_REVIEWED_RULE", "warrant": {"kind": "DEFINITIONAL_DERIVATION", "review_id": "native-monetary-unit-quantity-proposal-2026-11-01", "reviewer": "Codex primary source-backed proposal; not independent semantic gold", "source_refs": ["docs/readings/2026-11-01-lexicon-next-stage/quantity-unit-population-inventory.json@sha256:5a392a773cef5cebd2e9d05df34258bf17c35307cddd82d46be9dbb8134ced79", "docs/readings/2026-11-01-lexicon-you-body/you-body-reading.md", "gse/curation/lexicon_builder/foundation.py#projection_relations"], "statement": "Proposed scope: exact native noun senses with complete monetary_unit.n.01 ancestry and an explicitly attested native spelling. The 208 inspected native sense definitions and examples denote monetary units, fractional denominations, or denomination-bearing coin types. Their quantity content is intrinsic to the denomination, not the wealth or desirability of a referent. QUANTITY=+1 does not encode a particular amount, current exchange rate, size, value judgement, or ownership. A subtype whose own definition lacks quantitative denomination content falsifies this proposal. Anna (a former copper coin) and eurodollar (a deposited dollar used for international trade) are deliberately included as hard held-out audits. Morphology-derived spellings remain outside this rule until their identity is separately justified; no fallback signs apply. This is a GSE definitional projection interpreted from the native scope and measurement account, not an NSM-authored sign matrix. Source reading supports testing this proposed law; admission additionally requires independent withheld-answer model agreement across eight distinct senses and corpus replay.", "warrant_id": "native-monetary-unit-quantity-2026-11-01"}, "review": {"decision": "APPROVE_DEFINITIONAL_RULE", "rationale": "The complete native scope review found monetary denomina